Subject: Merge branch 'gpu-pass' into cpu-draw: the tiles' work beside the draws'

gpu-pass (92ed3e7) changes what a tiled pass is made of when it closes -- turnip's bins, bins for the attachments
the draws touch alone, the draws as draw-state groups, a fetch's barrier as a group, tiles or sysmem by what a pass
holds; cpu-draw changes how a draw's words are made. They meet in one line of CommandBuffer::draw and in the fake.

Conflicts, and how each was settled:
- src/render.cpp, CommandBuffer::draw: gmemPlan is called with gpu-pass's flag (kGmemOldTiles); why a draw cannot
  be tiled is said by this branch's whyNotTiled() (the reason is made only where it is kept).
- src/fake_gpu.cpp: both branches made the fake judge a fetch's bin by GMEM's own address (kGmemBase); gpu-pass's
  lines, which also note that the draw reads GMEM.
- include/hakios-metal/fake_gpu.hpp: both sides' additions kept (the submit hook and named(), the constants held
  to their program; the draw log, the constants' store).
- tests/render_test.cpp: four places where this branch had written the A610's numbers for the old bins beside the
  A635's; gpu-pass replaced those tests with ones of turnip's layout for both chips. Theirs.
- tools/dev.mk: src/gmem.cpp among the core's sources.

What holds the two together:
- closePass reads the pass's recorded draws (render::drawStates) and makes the groups from them. A draw taken from
  a kept state leaves the words a draw written whole leaves, so the groups are the same either way: the golden
  streams are the same from kept states (each draw checked, and unchecked) and written whole, both chips, and the
  random frames agree in tiles as in sysmem.
- tests/golden.hpp follows CP_SET_DRAW_STATE into each group's fragment, so that the words and the loads a binned
  pass keeps there are summed as a body's are (without it a binned pass's loads were not in the sums at all).
- tests/golden/ written again: the scenes drawn in tiles change (B, which reads its target, is now tiled; C, F,
  P, Q, K), the sysmem scenes are word for word what they were. drawbench --each against the base's draw path
  (b935418): sysmem and the plug-in's default the same for 184 programs of 184; forced tiles differ, as meant.

280 tests, 0 failed checks, with either chip's constants (269 of this branch, 11 of gpu-pass).


